<DocsLayout title="gRPC Reference">
  <h1>gRPC Reference</h1>
  <p>
    All RPCs live on the single service
    <code>identity.IdentityService</code>. The wire transports is
    Connect-RPC over HTTP/JSON; the underlying schema is plain protobuf.
    Method paths take the shape
    <code>/identity.IdentityService/&lt;Method&gt;</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The canonical schema lives at
    <a href="https://github.com/elloloop/identity/blob/main/proto/identity/identity.proto"><code>proto/identity/identity.proto</code></a>.
    This page summarises the surface; consult the .proto for exact field
    types and reservations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Proto changes are checked by Buf in CI. Pull requests must pass
    <code>buf lint</code> and a breaking-change check against
    <code>main</code>, so wire-compatible additions are allowed but removed
    fields, changed field numbers, renamed RPCs, and changed field types are
    blocked before merge.
  </p>

  <h2>Authentication</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>BeginOAuthLogin</code></td><td>none</td><td>Mint OAuth state + PKCE artifacts and return the provider authorization URL</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>OAuthLogin</code></td><td>none</td><td>Exchange the authorization code, validate provider identity, upsert the user, and issue tokens</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>PasswordSignup</code></td><td>none</td><td>Create user with email + password</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>PasswordLogin</code></td><td>none</td><td>Email + password → tokens (or TOTP challenge)</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Session / token</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GetCurrentUser</code></td><td>optional bearer</td><td>Return the caller's profile, or empty if unauthenticated</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RefreshToken</code></td><td>none</td><td>Rotate a refresh token to fresh access + refresh</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Logout</code></td><td>none</td><td>Revoke a single refresh token</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>UpdateProfile</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Self-service name / avatar update</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Password management</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ChangePassword</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Old + new password</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RequestPasswordReset</code></td><td>none</td><td>Send recovery-email reset link (no enumeration)</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Admin help</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RequestAdminHelp</code></td><td>none</td><td>User raises a "can't log in" ticket</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ListHelpRequests</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Paginated, filterable list</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ResolveHelpRequest</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Resolve or reject a ticket</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Passkey</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>BeginPasskeyRegistration</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Start enrollment (returns options + challenge)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>CompletePasskeyRegistration</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Persist the credential</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>BeginPasskeyLogin</code></td><td>none</td><td>Start authentication ceremony</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>CompletePasskeyLogin</code></td><td>none</td><td>Verify assertion, issue tokens</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ListPasskeys</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>List the caller's passkeys</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>DeletePasskey</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Remove a passkey by credential ID</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>QR cross-device login</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>InitiateQrLogin</code></td><td>none</td><td>New device requests a session</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GetQrLoginSession</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Authenticated device looks up the session for display</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ApproveQrLogin</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Authenticated device approves or rejects</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>PollQrLogin</code></td><td>none</td><td>New device polls for completion (returns tokens once approved)</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>2FA / TOTP</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>BeginTotpSetup</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Issue secret + recovery codes</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>VerifyTotpSetup</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Confirm enrollment with a code</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>DisableTotp</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Turn 2FA off (requires password)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>VerifyTotp</code></td><td>none</td><td>Complete a pending login challenge</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RegenerateRecoveryCodes</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>New batch of 10 (requires password)</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Sessions</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ListMySessions</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>List the caller's sessions</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RevokeSession</code></td><td>bearer</td><td>Revoke one by ID</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RevokeAllSessions</code></td><td>bearer + password</td><td>Revoke all the caller's sessions</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SignOutEverywhere</code></td><td>bearer + password</td><td>Same as above; named for clarity in UIs</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Audit</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ListAuditEvents</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Cursor-paginated, filterable by actor / target / type / time range</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Users</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>CreateUser</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Direct create</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GetUser</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Fetch one</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>UpdateUser</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Edit name / avatar / role</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>DeleteUser</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Hard delete</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ListUsers</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Paginated; filter and search</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Groups + membership</h2>
  <p>
    These RPCs manage identity-owned group and membership data. They do
    not make group membership an authorization decision for other RPCs or
    downstream resources.
  </p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>CreateGroup</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Create a group record</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>UpdateGroup</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Edit a group's name or description</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>DeleteGroup</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Delete a group record</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ListGroups</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Paginated list of groups</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>AddGroupMember</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Create a membership edge from user to group</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RemoveGroupMember</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Delete a membership edge from user to group</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ListGroupMembers</code></td><td>admin</td><td>List the users currently attached to a group</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Admin user management</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Auth</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>InviteUser</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Send invite, or create + return temp password</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>AcceptInvitation</code></td><td>none</td><td>User redeems invitation token</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>DeactivateUser</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Disable a user</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ReactivateUser</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Re-enable</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ResetUserPassword</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Temp password or reset token</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SetUserQuota</code></td><td>admin</td><td>Set <code>quota_bytes</code></td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Calling Connect-RPC over JSON</h2>
  <Code code={`# Generic shape — every RPC is a POST to /identity.IdentityService/<Method>
curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/PasswordLogin \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"email":"alice@example.com","password":"..."}'`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>Field naming</h2>
  <p>
    Connect's JSON codec uses camelCase by default:
    <code>access_token</code> on the wire becomes
    <code>accessToken</code> in JSON. Both forms are accepted on input.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
